== C5 Existing ids and behaviour kept: FAIL
Ids: PASS. Compared id= sets of GET /whatif, base vs branch, same fixture: removed [], 12 added (all *-exact / portfolio-value-exact), no duplicates, no count changes.
Live display while dragging in-card: PASS (C4 rows). Spending preview live on in-card inflation drag: PASS, same as base (preview.js: net 3.6% -> 1.8% -> 4.3%).
Three regressions, each proven with base vs branch on the same fixture (drag.baseA.json vs drag.brA.json):
- R1, the portfolio range select no longer drives the Quick Adjust portfolio slider. Before, updatePortfolioRange set the named range and syncQuickAdjustMirrorControls copied min/max/step to #qa-portfolio-value. Now the canonical control is a hidden input with no min/max/step, so nothing is copied.
  - On load (select = $0-5M): base qa max=5000000 step=50000; branch qa max=20000000 step=100000.
  - After the QA select is set to $0-1M: base qa max=1000000 step=10000; branch qa max=20000000 step=100000. Dragging then saves 12,800,000 while the select reads "$0-1M".
  - After the in-card select is set to $0-1M: same result.
- R2, dragging the QA investment-return mirror no longer updates the display live. Branch mid-drag samples at 3 and 6.5 both still show "Fixed 9.0% (overrides allocation)", corrected only after the save's swap. Base shows "Fixed 3.0%" then "Fixed 6.5%". Cause: updateInvestmentReturnDisplay lived in the canonical range's inline oninput; the canonical control is now a hidden input, and formatQuickAdjustDisplay skips 'investment-return'.
- R3, dragging the QA portfolio mirror no longer updates the per-account $ amounts (#td/#roth/#taxable-amount-display). Branch mid-drag values stay stale at [$639K,$4K,$127K] while the portfolio goes to $2,000,000 then $5,400,000. Base updates live ([$83K,$0,$17K] -> [$224K,$0,$46K]). Cause: updateAccountAmounts was in the canonical range's oninput.
  - Not checkable: the same mechanism would also skip updateSpendingPreview on QA inflation/decline drags. The preview panel closes on every save swap on both builds, so a live QA comparison could not be made.

