== (iii) formatExact on edge-case floats
formatExact outputs (temp test calling the real function, runtime floats), all ParseFloat back to the same float:
- 1e7 -> "10000000"
- 1e21 -> "1000000000000000000000"
- 1e-7 -> "0.0000001"
- 0.1+0.2 -> "0.30000000000000004"
- -0 -> "-0"
Chromium, `<input type=number step=any min=0 value=...>` (numaccept.js): every string valid, value kept, FormData carries the exact string, form checkValidity true. "-0" is accepted and valueAsNumber is 0.
D4, introduced by this diff: social-security.html renders COLA as `formatExact (mul COLARate 100)`, which exposes float noise in a visible number field.
- Stored 0.028 (the 2025 COLA), curl GET /whatif: branch `value="2.8000000000000003"`, base `value="2.8"`.
- Other stored values: 0.029 -> "2.9000000000000004"; 0.059 -> "5.8999999999999995"; 0.07 -> "7.000000000000001".
- An untouched submit saves 0.028000000000000004, a 1-ulp drift (0.026 does the same). It does not accumulate, stays under the oracle's 1e-9, and base drifted too (to 0.027999999999999997). The user-visible text is new.

